# Define a multi-tool capability profile

## Scope and existing evidence

Add colors, highlighters, automatic tool changes, cleaning, verification, and
resume rules without changing the accepted single-pen plan contract.

## Optional four-tool capability extension

**Inputs:** immutable single-pen plan identity; explicitly selected optional
`atrament.multi-tool/1` capability, calibrated tool IDs/offsets, verified
slot-to-tool mapping, available colors, marker/pen contact forces, clearance
and exclusion envelopes, cleaning status and original page/ink requirements.
**Outputs:** one proposed multi-tool schedule and typed preflight/refusals,
not an automatic motion program. Single-pen v1 capability and its schema
remain unchanged and default when the extension is absent.

**Profile example:** `ToolA` is a black fine pen; `ToolB` is a blue fine pen;
`ToolC` is a yellow highlighter; `ToolD` is reserved/empty. Tool IDs are
not merely RGB values: each binds measured offset, tip geometry, contact
height, drying group, support tier and docking slot. Proposed sequence:
black title, black prose, deliberate pen-up docking, verify `ToolB`, draw
blue border, then verify `ToolC` and place one highlight only after the
relevant text has admitted drying clearance. An unavailable tool is an
explicit `Unconvertible` item, never automatic substitution of black ink.

**Tool-change gate:** before every change verify all of pen-up state,
stationary and known XY, safe park path, collision-free rack/pen envelopes,
firmware/driver authority, current dock identity, tip cleanliness, and an
explicit operator-authorized tool request. Release and pickup each create
separate checkpoints, and the selected tool must be reidentified at the
post-pickup checkpoint. No deposition may occur during a dock transition.

**Recovery/refusal:** `WrongTool`, `ToolMissing`, `OffsetUnknown`,
`CleaningRequired`, `CollisionEnvelopeUnknown`, `DryingEvidenceMissing`,
`UncertainDockState`, or `PartialInkStroke` stops the proposed schedule.
On a crash or power loss, assume neither carriage coordinates nor active
pen is known; require human inspection, home/calibration and renewed
operator authorization. Do not replay a tool-change sequence or skip an
unsupported highlighter without explicit semantic acceptance.

**Compatibility boundary:** the proposed extension compiles only when
its caller explicitly opts in. A single-pen device continues to receive
its existing pen-up/down plan unchanged, with unsupported color/tool
requirements diagnosed one-by-one rather than erased. Hardware actions,
file exports, calibration and verification remain separate authorities.

**Assumptions and risks:** no actual tool encoder, slot sensor, color
calibration, ink drying model, maintenance robot or multi-tool machine has
been implemented. A profile field claiming a verified tool does not prove a
sensor observed it. This contract cannot arm a device.

## Acceptance decision

- **Basis:** theoretical optional capability extension, 2026-11-02.
- **Delivered:** one four-slot profile with explicit tool selection, colors,
  marker use, dock/cleaning/geometry gates, and uncertain-state refusals.
- **Unavailable:** actual multi-tool motion, measured calibration, sensors,
  highlighter reliability, collision guarantees or physical certification.
